      "event": "Extreme Heat Watch",
      "headline": "Extreme Heat Watch issued September 30 at 3:05AM PDT until October 7 at 9:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
      "description": "* WHAT...Dangerously hot conditions with high temperatures on the\nhottest days ranging from around 90 near the coast to the upper 90s\nto 108 for the valleys possible. Low temperatures for coastal areas\ninto the western valleys will warm into the lower to mid 70s during\nthe weekend with those warm overnight temperatures continuing for\nnext week.\n\n* WHERE...Orange County Coastal Areas, Orange County Inland Areas,\nSan Bernardino and Riverside County Valleys-The Inland Empire, San\nDiego County Coastal Areas, San Diego County Valleys, and Santa Ana\nMountains and Foothills.\n\n* WHEN...From Friday morning through Wednesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heat related illnesses increase significantly during\nextreme heat events.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A long-duration heat wave is expected to\ndevelop late this week and continue through much of next week into\nthe following weekend with Moderate or greater HeatRisk for the\ncoast and valleys and Major to Extreme HeatRisk for inland coastal\nareas into the western valleys.",
      "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.",
      "severity": "Severe",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "urgency": "Future",
